+[Term]
+id: UBERON:1200007
+name: submandibular gland ducto-acinar unit
+def: "A salivary gland ducto-acinar unit that is part of the submandibular gland, consisting of a mixture of predominantly serous acini (approximately 90%) with a minority of mucous acini, together with their contiguous ductal segments, and associated myoepithelial cells, stromal tissue, and vasculature. This unit produces a mixed serous-mucous saliva." [PMID:24862590, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK538325/]
+subset: added_by_HRA
